  "title": "The Four Verbs",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "cb7-l1",
      "title": "SUBTRACT and MULTIPLY",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "COBOL has a verb for each kind of arithmetic. SUBTRACT DISCOUNT FROM PRICE takes the discount off. MULTIPLY QTY BY PRICE would put the result into PRICE.",
        "Usually you want to keep the inputs, so there's GIVING: MULTIPLY QTY BY PRICE GIVING TOTAL. It works with ADD and SUBTRACT too: ADD A B GIVING C, SUBTRACT A FROM B GIVING C.",
        "With GIVING, the result can also go into an edited field directly, ready to print."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. SHOP.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 QTY        PIC 9(2)    VALUE 3.",
          "       01 PRICE      PIC 9(3)V99 VALUE 8.90.",
          "       01 DISCOUNT   PIC 9(3)V99 VALUE 1.70.",
          "       01 TOTAL      PIC 9(4)V99.",
          "       01 TOTAL-OUT  PIC $$$9.99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           MULTIPLY QTY BY PRICE GIVING TOTAL.",
          "           SUBTRACT DISCOUNT FROM TOTAL.",
          "           MOVE TOTAL TO TOTAL-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"3 PIZZAS: \" TOTAL-OUT.",
          "           ADD TOTAL 2.50 GIVING TOTAL-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"DELIVERED:\" TOTAL-OUT.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "3 PIZZAS:  $25.00",
          "DELIVERED: $27.50"
        ]
      },
