    {
      "id": "cb7-l3",
      "title": "ROUNDED and SIZE ERROR",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Results are cut, not rounded: 2.999 into PIC 9V99 is 2.99. Add ROUNDED after the field, and COBOL rounds instead: 3.00.",
        "When a result is too big for its field, the front digits are lost without warning. ON SIZE ERROR catches that: the field is left as it was, and your statements run instead.",
        "NOT ON SIZE ERROR runs when everything fit. END-ADD (or END-MULTIPLY …) closes the statement."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. SAFE.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 TWO        PIC 9    VALUE 2.",
          "       01 CUT-RES    PIC 9V99.",
          "       01 ROUND-RES  PIC 9V99.",
          "       01 SMALL      PIC 999  VALUE 100.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           DIVIDE 3 INTO TWO GIVING CUT-RES.",
          "           DIVIDE 3 INTO TWO GIVING ROUND-RES ROUNDED.",
          "           DISPLAY \"CUT \" CUT-RES \"  ROUNDED \" ROUND-RES.",
          "           ADD 950 TO SMALL",
          "               ON SIZE ERROR DISPLAY \"TOO BIG, NOT CHANGED: \" SMALL",
          "               NOT ON SIZE ERROR DISPLAY \"OK: \" SMALL",
          "           END-ADD.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "CUT 066  ROUNDED 067",
          "TOO BIG, NOT CHANGED: 100"
        ]
      },
